 "text": "John buys twice as many red ties as blue ties.  The red ties cost 50% more than blue ties.  He spent $200 on blue ties that cost $40 each. How much did he spend on ties?\nHe bought 200 / 40 = 5 blue ties\nSo he bought 5 * 2 = 10 red ties\nEach red tie cost $40 * .5 = $20 more than blue ties\nSo they each cost $40 + $20 = $60\nSo he spent $60 * 10 = $600 on red ties\nSo he spent $200 + $600 = $800 on ties\nThe final answer is 800",
